  * WebAssembly/wabt — instruction-table data

    Copyright 2016 WebAssembly Community Group participants
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (third_party/wabt/LICENSE).

    wasmrt's WebAssembly instruction data is derived from wabt, by way of
    binaryang's shared definitions (definitions/binaryang/). It is generated
    into crates/wasmrt-core/src/tables.rs, which IS part of every wasmrt
    binary (opcode-to-proposal gating, and the SIMD and atomic mnemonic
    tables), and into crates/wasmrt-core/src/definitions.rs, which is compiled
    only for tests. Both generated files carry this attribution and a change
    note. wabt ships no NOTICE file of its own.

    The wasmrt engine itself is 100% original Rust and ships its OWN C ABI
    header ("wasmrt.h"); it does NOT vendor the standard wasm-c-api "wasm.h"
    that the source project wazmrt vendored.
